# Release workflow

Use when the user asks to prepare a release, bump the extension version, update the changelog for a cut, package a VSIX before publish, or create a version tag.

## Source of truth

1. Follow `.cursor/skills/prepare-release/SKILL.md` step by step.
2. Align git/tag and GitHub Release expectations with `RELEASE.md`.

## Files to keep in sync

- Bump **`apps/vscode/package.json`** (the only place the extension `version` lives; the root `package.json` has no `version` field) and the single root **`package-lock.json`** (`packages["apps/vscode"].version`) to the same target version.
- Add or finalize **`apps/vscode/CHANGELOG.md`** and **`apps/vscode/CHANGELOG.en.md`** (dated `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section; move items out of `[Unreleased]` when cutting). Version update requests must update both changelog files in the same change.

## After verification

Run the scripts from the root `package.json` listed in the skill (typically `compile`, `lint`, `test`, `build`, `package:vsix` when packaging); `compile` and `package:vsix` are extension-only; `build`, `lint` and `test` fan out to all three apps.

Create **`git tag v<version>`** and push only after the maintainer confirms; the tag must match the **root** `package.json` version with a leading `v`, and every app must already be synced to it (`node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check`). One tag ships the VSIX, the bot tarball and the CLI tarball.
